<title>JAPAN: NTT eyes $500 mln investment in French market -- FT.</title>
<headline>NTT eyes $500 mln investment in French market -- FT.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) is considering making an investment of $500 million in the French telecoms markets, Britain's Financial Times reported on Thursday,</p>
<p>The paper said the Japanese telecoms giant is considering investing $500 million to buy 10 percent of French carrier Cetel, which is a unit of Cie Generale des Eaux, and seen as the main rival to France Telecom.</p>
<p>NTT declined to say whether it is mulling the potential acquisition. &quot;It is too early to say anything,&quot; an NTT official said when asked about the report.</p>
</text>
